# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 usual.cc asinasln, asinhasln, after patch 0020. asin(i*y) for a real y, and asinh(i*y) for a real y with |y| <= 1, are purely imaginary, but the ln form (and patch 0020's rounding of it at a raised precision, small_cplx_ln_form) leaves its rounding in the real part, and evalf shows it: evalf(asinh(i/10)) at Digits 12 in our CAS view was -1.18694596822E-66+0.100167421162*i, evalf(asin(i/10^20)) -9.87065545841E-86+1E-20*i, evalf(asin(i/3)) -5.1E-61+0.327450150237*i (Giac's own asin of a complex MPFR value left such a part before patch 0020 too, 4.1E-61 for asin(i/10)). Now, where the real part of x is exactly 0 (an exact 0 or an MPFR zero), the result is i times the imaginary part of the rounded result, with a real part that is a zero of the imaginary part's type (an MPFR zero beside an MPFR part, as Giac's own evalf(i/3) has: an exact 0 there made asinh(5*asin(i/3)) a double); for asinh only when |im(x)| <= 1, where asinh(i*y) = i*asin(y).
